[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974500627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116857#issuecomment-3974500627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116857","id":3974500627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s5hET","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T18:47:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T18:47:17Z","body":"What defines this type normally?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974500627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974572064","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116857#issuecomment-3974572064","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116857","id":3974572064,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s5ygg","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T19:02:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T19:02:17Z","body":"Looks like it's normally defined by `unknwn.h`, which is given a proper include here:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/95535167b33975afa4e82228eb71800d36cf51dd/thirdparty/openxr/src/common/xr_dependencies.h#L33-L34\r\nStrangely, none of the files in `thirdparty/openxr/include` appear to forward-declare this, so I'm not sure where this is intended to be added. Though this whole module seems wonky with how platform-specific stuff is front-loaded, so I could've missed something?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974572064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975046341","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116857#issuecomment-3975046341","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116857","id":3975046341,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s7mTF","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T20:54:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T20:54:29Z","body":"Do we need `windows.h` at all here, `unknwn.h` seems to be sufficient to build it (only tested cross-build with clang).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975046341/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975108155","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116857#issuecomment-3975108155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116857","id":3975108155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s71Y7","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T21:10:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T21:20:13Z","body":"`windows.h` is included in `unknwn.h`. I assumed that would mean the library version is used, but it actually seems to still prefer our override!\r\n\r\nI assume the forward-declare is still preferable for a header; I'll see if that can be taken any further\r\n\r\n**EDIT:** Maaaybe, but digging any further would be beyond the scope of this PR. Will integrate this as-is","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975108155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975175081","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116857#issuecomment-3975175081","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116857","id":3975175081,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s8Fup","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T21:29:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T21:29:23Z","body":"> windows.h is included in unknwn.h. I assumed that would mean the library version is used, but it actually seems to still prefer our override!\r\n\r\nWindows headers are horrible mess, but it should be possible to limit it to only COM interface stuff.\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n#define COM_NO_WINDOWS_H\r\n#include <objbase.h>\r\n#include <unknwn.h>\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs this error reproducible locally? I have seen it randomly showing up in CI builds, but no with my own builds. I assume it was caused by forcing `WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN` globally with new `windows.h` wrapper, which was not set in OpenXR, but it's strange it's not always reproducible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975175081/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975196706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116857#issuecomment-3975196706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116857","id":3975196706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s8LAi","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T21:35:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T21:35:00Z","body":"The error was reproducable with `d3d12=no` locally, though adding the forward-declare fixed it. However:\r\n> ```cpp\r\n> #define COM_NO_WINDOWS_H\r\n> #include <objbase.h>\r\n> #include <unknwn.h>\r\n> ```\r\nThis *also* fixed it, and in a way that lets us ditch `windows.h` outright!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3975196706/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]